diff --git a/docs/CHIKLETS.md b/docs/CHIKLETS.md
index 2b22b35..c2d91fd 100644
--- a/docs/CHIKLETS.md
+++ b/docs/CHIKLETS.md
@@ -1,6 +1,62 @@
 # Chiklet authoring
 
-Each file under `chiklets/` is one self-service operation. Required top-level keys are `id`, `version`, `name`, `description`, `icon`, `allowed_server_groups`, `form_schema` and `foreman`.
+Each JSON file directly under `chiklets/` is one self-service operation. Required top-level keys are `id`, `version`, `name`, `description`, `icon`, `allowed_server_groups`, `form_schema` and `foreman`.
+
+The catalogue is read from the mounted `chiklets/` directory at request time and each definition is cached by file modification time. Adding, changing or removing a JSON file therefore does not require a container restart or rebuild.
+
+## Server-group scope
+
+Use explicit server-group slugs when a Chiklet is restricted:
+
+```json
+"allowed_server_groups": ["linux-dev", "linux-uat"]
+```
+
+Use the wildcard when the Chiklet is available in every server group:
+
+```json
+"allowed_server_groups": ["*"]
+```
+
+`*` affects Chiklet availability only. It never grants host access. The destination list and submission endpoint still enforce the signed-in user's server-group membership. A global administrator can target any enabled server in a group allowed by the Chiklet. The wildcard must be used by itself; `['*', 'linux-dev']` is rejected as ambiguous configuration.
+
+## Icons and hot-loadable assets
+
+Legacy text/emoji icons continue to work:
+
+```json
+"icon": "DB"
+```
+
+For a local image, place the asset under `chiklets/assets/` and reference it by relative filename:
+
+```text
+chiklets/
+├── install-mssql-odbc-driver.json
+└── assets/
+    └── mssql.svg
+```
+
+```json
+"icon": {
+  "type": "image",
+  "src": "mssql.svg",
+  "alt": "Microsoft SQL Server"
+}
+```
+
+SVG, PNG, JPG/JPEG and WebP are supported. Asset paths are restricted to the Chiklet asset directory and path traversal is rejected. Images are served with no-cache headers so replacing the file is reflected without rebuilding the web image. Existing same-origin absolute paths such as `/static/...` are also accepted, although files added to the image's built-in static directory still require an image rebuild.
+
+A structured text icon is also supported:
+
+```json
+"icon": {
+  "type": "text",
+  "value": "DB"
+}
+```
+
+## Form schema
 
 The form uses JSON Schema Draft 2020-12. The built-in renderer supports strings, integers, numbers, booleans, enums, enum arrays and multiline strings. Backend JSON Schema validation is authoritative.
 
